00:10:05,530 --> 00:10:10,530
Question 2. Traditional crafts
that were previously declining.

106
00:10:11,110 --> 00:10:13,250
Alright, let's look for our keywords.

107
00:10:13,810 --> 00:10:18,950
In the second sentence of paragraph 3, we
see traditional crafts mentioned directly.

108
00:10:19,510 --> 00:10:22,810
Also, keep an eye on the phrase previously declining.

109
00:10:23,470 --> 00:10:26,810
In the text, this is paraphrased as dying out.

110
00:10:27,050 --> 00:10:29,810
This confirms we are in the right spot.

111
00:10:30,070 --> 00:10:34,850
The passage tells us that these crafts have been brought back because tourists

112
00:10:34,850 --> 00:10:38,190
want to buy authentic handmade products.

113
00:10:38,950 --> 00:10:40,150
Now look at our endings.

114
00:10:40,670 --> 00:10:42,930
Ending B is a perfect match.

115
00:10:43,570 --> 00:10:43,690
Why?

116
00:10:44,550 --> 00:10:50,370
Because successfully revived means the same thing as brought back and demand

117
00:10:50,370 --> 00:10:56,550
for authentic items matches the part about
tourists paying for authentic products.

118
00:10:57,100 --> 00:11:01,090
So, our final sentence is

119
00:11:01,090 --> 00:11:06,150
Traditional crafts that were previously declining have been successfully

120
00:11:06,150 --> 00:11:11,350
revived through tourist demand for authentic items.

121
00:11:11,790 --> 00:11:13,550
Our answer is B.

122
00:11:15,250 --> 00:11:18,510
Question 3. Exposure to foreign visitors.

123
00:11:18,970 --> 00:11:21,310
Scan the start of paragraph 4.

124
00:11:21,310 --> 00:11:26,330
You'll see, influx of foreign visitors exposes local residents.

125
00:11:27,190 --> 00:11:31,710
This matches our keyword exposure to foreign visitors perfectly.

126
00:11:32,030 --> 00:11:34,410
So the answer must be right here.

127
00:11:34,910 --> 00:11:40,750
The text says it can create generational conflicts because elderly community

128
00:11:40,750 --> 00:11:45,710
members worry that younger residents are leaving their traditions behind.

129
00:11:46,250 --> 00:11:47,890
Now let's check the endings.

130
00:11:47,890 --> 00:11:50,850
Ending E stands out immediately.

131
00:11:51,470 --> 00:11:56,610
The phrase cause tensions is just another way to say create conflicts.

132
00:11:57,090 --> 00:12:02,970
And between younger and older generations is exactly what the text describes

133
00:12:02,970 --> 00:12:05,510
with the elderly and the youth.

134
00:12:06,010 --> 00:12:11,830
So when we put it together, exposure to foreign visitors may cause tensions

135
00:12:11,830 --> 00:12:14,030
between younger and older generations.

136
00:12:14,730 --> 00:12:16,070
The answer is E.

